### Remaining verification limits and recommendations

The present 14 pure test bodies cover the baseline, several core A–G cases, first-match/default denial, some unsupported inputs and replay. They do not yet permanently retain all of the independent probe cases above. Add focused regressions for source-return receiving direction, selected shadow return, exact wrong hub identity, NSG Unknown, reverse-initiation Deny and combined-budget/subtype preservation; these are substantive edge cases, not mirrored implementation assertions. Per-family capacity boundaries and priority endpoints also remain reviewable test gaps in the submitted file even though their validators are straightforward on inspection.

No real PostgreSQL, schema migration, browser/keyboard/Axe/visual, complete regression, stamp, CI/strict, preview-SHA or human SME result was independently executed in this follow-up. The four integration test bodies were reviewed, not counted as reviewer passes. Future source changes require their own affected recheck and the planned fresh final post-stamp audit.

